    "created_at": "2026-11-22T14:15:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T14:15:46Z",
    "body": "Cause found for the uma stop at 13:47 UTC (run of `49aaaaa60`, #3440): **systemd-oomd killed the runner's service**, not a CamCraft failure. From uma's journal (runner user unit):\n\n```\n05:47:49 uma systemd[1723]: actions-runner.service: systemd-oomd killed some process(es) in this unit.\n05:47:49 uma systemd[1723]: actions-runner.service: Main process exited, code=killed, status=9/KILL\n```\n\numa (61 GB) was running the gate's build while our pool builds were still running on the same host (the pause stops new pool jobs, not running ones), so memory pressure crossed oomd's limit and it picked the runner's cgroup. Nothing was logged because the whole unit was SIGKILLed, which matches \"no conclusion and no log\".\n\nMitigation applied on uma (mkinney side): the pool user's slice is capped (`user-<uid>.slice MemoryHigh=30G MemoryMax=40G`), so under pressure the pool builds are throttled or killed first and the runner keeps its memory. The skull 63-minute hang is still open; next step there is the same journal check for that time window.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
